# Native Libraries Directory

This directory contains pre-built llama.cpp native libraries for each platform.

## Directory Structure

```
natives/
├── macos-arm64/
│   └── libllama.dylib
├── macos-x64/
│   └── libllama.dylib
├── linux-x64/
│   └── libllama.so
├── linux-arm64/
│   └── libllama.so
└── windows-x64/
    └── llama.dll
```

## Building Libraries

Run the GitHub Actions workflow `build-llama-cpp.yml` to build all libraries:

1. Go to Actions → "Build llama.cpp Native Libraries"
2. Click "Run workflow"
3. Enter the llama.cpp version (e.g., `b4239`)
4. Download the `llama-natives-all` artifact
5. Extract and copy libraries to this directory

## Manual Build

To build manually for your platform:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/ggerganov/llama.cpp
cd llama.cpp
cmake -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON
cmake --build build --config Release
```

Then copy the resulting library to the appropriate directory.
